A straight-chain representation of the glucose molecule showing carbon atoms numbered 1 through 6.
*   **Carbon 1:** Has a double bond to Oxygen (C=O) and a single bond to Hydrogen (H). This is labeled the **ALDEHYDE GROUP**.
*   **Carbon 2:** Has an -OH group and -H.
*   **Carbon 3:** Has an -OH group (highlighted in red) and -H.
*   **Carbon 4:** Has an -OH group and -H.
